{
  "name": "When Is It Time to Get a Professional Roof Assessment?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: You're Seeing Recurring Leaks or Water Stains",
      "text": "If you've noticed water stains on your ceiling or walls, or have had multiple leaks, even small ones, it's a clear sign. These aren't just cosmetic issues; they can indicate serious underlying problems with your roof's integrity, flashing, or decking that need immediate professional attention.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Widespread Deterioration or Visible Damage",
      "text": "Are shingles curling, cracking, or losing granules? Is there visible damage from hail or wind? If the wear and tear is widespread and not just isolated, it's time for a pro to assess the full extent of the damage. What looks like minor surface wear can often hide deeper issues.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Suspect Concealed Moisture or Structural Sagging",
      "text": "Sometimes the problems aren't on the surface. If you notice a sagging roofline, or suspect moisture in your attic (even without visible leaks), a professional can use specialized techniques to detect hidden issues before they cause structural damage or mold.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Buying or Selling a Property",
      "text": "When you're involved in a real estate transaction, a comprehensive roof assessment is invaluable. It provides peace of mind for buyers and sellers alike, identifying potential issues that could affect the property's value or future maintenance costs.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: After a Major Storm or Severe Weather Event",
      "text": "Even if you don't see obvious damage, a strong Texas storm with high winds or hail can cause unseen damage that can shorten your roof's life. A professional inspection after such an event can identify and address these issues proactively.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 6: Your Roof is Nearing Its Estimated Lifespan",
      "text": "If your roof is getting close to its typical lifespan (e.g., asphalt shingles around 15-20 years), a professional assessment can help you plan for future repairs or replacement, giving you options before an emergency forces your hand. If any of these sound familiar, don't wait. Contact Discounted Roofing Co. for a thorough, honest assessment and clear recommendations.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 6
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": [
      "h1",
      ".howto-step",
      "[itemprop=\"step\"]"
    ]
  },
